###4.list all the container
docker ps -a
• Terminal output arrows:
	• CONTAINER ID \(\rightarrow \) Container ID
	• IMAGE \(\rightarrow \) Base Image
	• COMMAND \(\rightarrow \) Bash Terminal
	• CREATED \(\rightarrow \) The container was created 2 min ago
	• NAMES \(\rightarrow \) container name (Two containers cannot have the same name)

Container runtime
	• Running \(\rightarrow \) utilize RAM, CPU & storage
	• Stopped \(\rightarrow \) Release CPU & RAM but storage is there. All the saved which was saved will be there but unsaved files is removed.
	• Paused \(\rightarrow \) Release the RAM

###5. stop the container
docker stop <container name> or <cont id>

###6. start the container
docker start <container name> or <cont id>

###7. we want to enter inside a existing container :
docker exec -t c01 /bin/bash

exec --> execute the existing container

###8. Remove a container :- note: u cannot remove a running container
docker stop c01
docker rm c01

###9.Remove the Image from local registry
docker rmi <image name>:<TAG version>
docker rmi ubuntu:latest                      \ubuntu -base image

note:if a image associated with any container you cannot directly delete the image
